1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,878
[♪ tense music playing]

2
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,635
Abaddon, get those angels away
from him now!

3
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:10,594
[Abaddon grunts]

4
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:13,764
[gasps worriedly]

5
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:15,974
[groaning]

6
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,143
Mister?

7
00:00:23,065 --> 00:00:25,359
[♪ opening theme song playing]

8
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:54,197
[train clattering in distance]

9
00:01:55,741 --> 00:01:58,368
[footsteps approaching]

10
00:01:58,452 --> 00:01:59,369
Huh?

11
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:02,539
Uh.

12
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:04,583
Hmm.

13
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:10,964
[YOUNG NEIGHBOR] This man
is the reason I'm alive.

14
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:12,215
♪

15
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:14,468
Without him,
I'd probably be dead,

16
00:02:15,177 --> 00:02:16,762
face down in some ditch.

17
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:20,557
I'm too young
to do much for myself.

18
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,269
I can't run away from my mother.

19
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:30,776
And I can't afford
to refuse his kindness.

20
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:42,996
[sighs]

21
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,542
What a pathetic creature I am.

22
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,173
Who even am I?

23
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,260
I feel like I'm slowly turning
into something that isn't me.

24
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,513
It's scary to think of.

25
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:05,102
Maybe it would be easier
to just give in.

26
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:07,896
Not again.

27
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:09,523
[sighs]

28
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:10,857
[YOUNG NEIGHBOR]
And somewhere along the way of

29
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:13,026
becoming someone who I'm not...

30
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:15,987
[grunts]

31
00:03:16,071 --> 00:03:17,239
[clatters]

32
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:19,616
[YOUNG NEIGHBOR]
...it hit me, an idea.

33
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,577
Damn it, damn it, damn it all.

34
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,579
Why do bad things
only happen to me?

35
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:25,914
Screw this.

36
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:28,917
[YOUNG NEIGHBOR]
If maybe, instead of

37
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,627
always being
on the receiving end,

38
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:31,962
I could repay him.

39
00:03:32,671 --> 00:03:35,549
Maybe that would be enough
to turn me back into me,

40
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,592
instead of this.

41
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:39,177
♪

42
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:42,681
The man next door
is deeply lonely,

43
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:44,266
just like me.

44
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:46,977
That's how I know...

45
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,857
he and I are the same.

46
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,365
Did he think so too?

47
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:03,827
Did he also see me
as a kindred spirit?

48
00:04:04,661 --> 00:04:06,830
That must be why
he looks after me.

49
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,001
It must be.

50
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,586
Just look at all he's doing.

51
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,546
And in that case...

52
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:17,924
I need to find some way
to pay him back.

53
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:23,263
But what can I give?

54
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:24,264
Hmm.

55
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,311
We were told
a young lady named Kurosu

56
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:31,438
lives in this apartment.
Would that happen to be you?

57
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:34,524
[MAN 2] Try to remain calm
while we tell you this.

58
00:04:34,608 --> 00:04:36,359
Your mother was hit by a car.

59
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:37,903
It doesn't look good.

60
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:40,113
-You mean it?
-[MAN 3] Yeah.

61
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:42,032
She's in a hospital nearby.

62
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,992
How about
we give you a ride there?

63
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,535
You can trust us.

64
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:47,037
The three of us
work very closely

65
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,747
with your mother every day.

66
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:49,915
How bad?

67
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,000
Is she going to be okay,
do you think?

68
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:54,544
The doctors say
it's still pretty touch and go.

69
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:55,754
Come along now.

70
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:57,088
We'll get you straight over
to see her.

71
00:04:57,172 --> 00:04:59,758
We're gonna
take good care of you.

72
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:01,134
Pardon me.

73
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:03,470
Who are you,
and why are you talking to her?

74
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:04,846
-Hmm?
-Eh?

75
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:06,473
We could ask you the same thing.

76
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,058
Well, I'm her father.

77
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,226
[all gasp]

78
00:05:10,936 --> 00:05:14,022
Hey, man. I thought you said
she didn't have a dad.

79
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,273
What do we do now?

80
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:17,484
[MAN 1] Uh, let me explain.

81
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:18,818
We work with your wife.

82
00:05:18,902 --> 00:05:20,445
I'm sure she would recognize us.

83
00:05:20,529 --> 00:05:22,239
May I ask
for the number of your office

84
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,241
and any extensions
to speak with your departments?

85
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:25,242
[man 1 gasps]

86
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:26,618
Also, give me the name

87
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,703
of each of
your respective superiors.

88
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:30,038
I'm sure
I'll be familiar with them.

89
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,915
My wife talks
at length about work.

90
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:33,917
[all gasp nervously]

91
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,545
Let's just get out of here.

92
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:39,005
[MAN 2] Had to
get in our way, huh?

93
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:40,215
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

94
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:41,174
-[man 2 grunts]
-[thuds]

95
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:42,467
[man 1, man 3 panting]

96
00:05:42,551 --> 00:05:43,677
[MAN 3] Let's get outta here.

97
00:05:45,846 --> 00:05:46,846
They hurt you.

98
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,808
Mister, tell me
they didn't get anywhere bad.

99
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:50,976
[Sasaki sighs]

100
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:52,978
I'm okay.

101
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:55,021
Lucky I thought ahead.

102
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:57,190
I had a magazine in there.

103
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,401
Plus this camera.

104
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:00,652
[gasps softly]

105
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:04,406
You're like an action hero
straight out of a movie

106
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:05,448
or an anime.

107
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:07,909
Oh? You really think so?
[chuckles]

108
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:11,580
[NEIGHBOR] Like a kid,

109
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:14,624
he had this bashful smile
that day.

110
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:18,503
I was too shy
to ask him anything else,

111
00:06:19,254 --> 00:06:20,130
but...

112
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,925
in my childish eyes,

113
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:27,053
he looked like the embodiment
of heroism.

114
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:30,432
And now, he saved me again.

115
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:34,102
Why did it have to come to this?

116
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:37,480
Mister, look at me!

117
00:06:39,316 --> 00:06:40,191
[SASAKI] Crap.

118
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:43,403
Where... are my legs?

119
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:52,203
[ABADDON] This is a rotten
matchup for us, don't you think?

120
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:54,748
[SASAKI] This doesn't look good.

121
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,417
My healing spell isn't working.

122
00:06:58,418 --> 00:06:59,502
[grunts]

123
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:03,548
Mister, you can't die.
Stay with me.

124
00:07:03,632 --> 00:07:06,760
I'm glad you're safe.
That's enough.

125
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:07,928
[neighbor crying]

126
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:10,221
I don't care what happens to me.

127
00:07:11,306 --> 00:07:12,474
It doesn't matter.

128
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,142
Nothing else matters

129
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:16,144
besides getting you
out of here alive.

130
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,145
[sobbing]

131
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,940
[gasps, yells]

132
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:22,734
-[grunts]
-[huffs]

133
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,154
-[grunts]
-[thuds]

134
00:07:33,328 --> 00:07:34,287
We should withdraw.

135
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,794
[Sasaki breathing weakly]

136
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:45,090
[NEIGHBOR] No,
I'm begging you, don't die!

137
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:46,716
-[crying]
-You need to go.

138
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,511
I want you to spend your years
living a life happy enough

139
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:50,553
for us both.

140
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:55,767
You're so young,
so much time left...

141
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,186
No. Please wake up.

142
00:07:58,269 --> 00:07:59,187
Don't leave me!

143
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,231
You can't! I couldn't!

144
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:02,774
I never repaid you!

145
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,818
I haven't done anything for you!

146
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:08,238
[crying]

147
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:15,245
[YOUNG NEIGHBOR] Mister, thanks
for what you did that day.

148
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:18,123
[SASAKI] I'm sure you already
heard the good news.

149
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:20,709
They caught those men,
the ones who bothered you.

150
00:08:20,792 --> 00:08:21,793
Thank you.

151
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:24,295
Is there any way I can repay you
for what you did?

152
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:25,839
Oh, no need.

153
00:08:26,631 --> 00:08:28,800
I mean it.
If there's anything I can do,

154
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,427
please just say it,

155
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,512
and I would do anything
that you want.

156
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:36,474
Hmm. Well,
if you really wanna pay me back,

157
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:38,268
I ordered a grocery delivery,

158
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:40,895
and I'm expecting it to arrive
sometime later today.

159
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,647
But wouldn't you know,
I got carried away

160
00:08:42,731 --> 00:08:43,898
and ordered too much.

161
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:45,608
Mm.

162
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:50,530
I mean, I wasn't talking
about stuff like that.

163
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:54,075
Isn't there anything I can do
to really help you?

164
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,119
Oh, I know.

165
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,540
It would help me a lot
if you took this off my hands.

166
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,376
That'll do.

167
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:04,544
See you later.

168
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:07,255
Have a good day.

169
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,801
He's everything.

170
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,803
The reason I'm alive.

171
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:18,058
But he only gives
and takes nothing back.

172
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,686
And that's eating away
at my self-worth.

173
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:26,191
But if I could
get off the receiving end,

174
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:28,401
if I could repay him...

175
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:32,697
maybe I'd be the real me again.

176
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,657
That's what I believe.

177
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:39,120
Until now, I've never known
what that would look like,

178
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:41,164
repaying him.

179
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,085
But having those degenerates
stare at me

180
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:47,629
gave me a realization.

181
00:09:49,047 --> 00:09:52,258
All I can offer... is my body.

182
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,219
So that's it.

183
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:57,263
I'll have to make use of that.

184
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:04,854
So now, I'll work on growing up.

185
00:10:05,647 --> 00:10:08,233
Wait for me until then, mister.

186
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:12,445
I know deep down,
you and I are the same.

187
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:16,616
We're both missing something,
but we'll fulfill each other.

188
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,576
Don't you agree, mister?

189
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,913
Right? I know you.

190
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:29,295
[grunts softly]

191
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:35,051
What? You're alive!

192
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:46,813
Hey, not to sound ungrateful,
but why do I have legs again?

193
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:48,815
[breathing shakily]

194
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:54,237
-You're all right! I'm so glad!
-[muffled grunting]

195
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:56,656
[laughing happily]

196
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:59,492
[SASAKI]
What in the world's going on?

197
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:02,453
[ABADDON] It's good
you can celebrate and all,

198
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:04,914
but why don't we spare a thought
for the time and place?

199
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:06,999
It is you.

200
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,418
[squelches]

201
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:13,756
Sup?

202
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:17,177
I guess this is your second time
meeting me in this form.

203
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:18,720
Huh?

204
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:24,267
Hmm.

205
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,435
Uh.

206
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:27,228
Excuse me.

207
00:11:27,312 --> 00:11:29,314
Where did that
multi-winged angel go?

208
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:32,191
I suppose they fled when I drove
their disciples off,

209
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:34,694
though I imagine they're
going to want some retribution,

210
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,945
and I shudder to think of

211
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:37,906
what they might send our way
the next time.

212
00:11:38,573 --> 00:11:41,117
Granted, I expect they'll be
keeping their distance

213
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:43,286
for a little while, now that
there's an unknown element

214
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:44,495
in the mix, like you.

215
00:11:44,579 --> 00:11:46,623
That would be the safest move
for them.

216
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:47,707
Uh.

217
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:50,335
[SASAKI] Going off
what a disciple told me,

218
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:52,337
that mysterious space
only manifests

219
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,838
when there are
a certain number of angels

220
00:11:53,922 --> 00:11:55,381
or demons in an area.

221
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,133
Can I assume then,

222
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:59,052
with the departure
of enough angels,

223
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:00,720
we were returned
to our normal world,

224
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:03,097
and that's the reason why
my body was healed to its state

225
00:12:03,181 --> 00:12:04,599
before the space appeared?

226
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:06,142
You're close.

227
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:08,728
You got the broader strokes,
but your details are off.

228
00:12:09,312 --> 00:12:10,647
[SASAKI] Is that so?

229
00:12:11,481 --> 00:12:13,107
[ABADDON] First,
it's not how many.

230
00:12:13,191 --> 00:12:15,693
Past that,
it's not the angels and demons,

231
00:12:15,777 --> 00:12:17,153
but their disciples.

232
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:20,114
Earlier, I must have
killed the angel's disciples

233
00:12:20,198 --> 00:12:23,034
or just drove them far enough
from the demon disciple,

234
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:25,370
AKA this girl
you happen to know,

235
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:27,580
making the quarantine space
dissipate.

236
00:12:28,206 --> 00:12:29,666
And because of that,

237
00:12:29,749 --> 00:12:32,585
I was narrowly able to
keep my intestines inside of me?

238
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:34,003
Then I have you to thank.

239
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:36,047
Well, it's only thanks to you

240
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,049
that my disciple
wasn't chopped into bits.

241
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,884
I'd say that makes us even.

242
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,844
Still, I didn't realize
how clueless you'd be

243
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:43,388
about the whole situation.

244
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,139
Not gonna argue there.

245
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:47,892
I would certainly
appreciate an explanation.

246
00:12:47,976 --> 00:12:49,185
I'd be happy to oblige,

247
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:50,895
as long as
you can make this conversation

248
00:12:50,979 --> 00:12:52,188
a two-way street.

249
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:53,481
What do you mean?

250
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:55,400
I believe I already explained

251
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,318
that you are
the unknown element here.

252
00:12:58,194 --> 00:12:59,320
[SASAKI] I see.

253
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:00,947
They're as confused as me.

254
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:04,325
Angels and demons don't know
about psychic powers.

255
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:06,619
And with my neighbor involved,

256
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:09,580
I don't wanna make an enemy
of this strange boy.

257
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:11,999
It seems like we're both lost.

258
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:13,334
Why don't we
share our information

259
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:14,377
between each other?

260
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:17,338
Yeah, I think that
sounds like a lovely idea.

261
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:19,465
Mister, thank you.

262
00:13:19,549 --> 00:13:21,134
I was happy to see you there.

263
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,802
You came at the perfect time.

264
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:26,139
No, I was just playing things
by ear. I got lucky.

265
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:28,558
Hey there!

266
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:30,143
Can I join you all over there?

267
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:32,353
Will anyone attack me?

268
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:35,106
Mister, do you know
that little girl?

269
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,357
Well, yes.

270
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:38,776
You could say she's kinda
like my coworker.

271
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:42,113
[NEIGHBOR] A coworker?
She seems so young.

272
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,198
[SASAKI] She's actually
older than you.

273
00:13:44,282 --> 00:13:45,992
Older than me, for that matter.

274
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,828
[gasps] How does that work?

275
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:52,957
Well, uh, I'll just include that
in my explanation later.

276
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:54,917
We shouldn't talk too much
out here.

277
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:56,961
Right. No problem.

278
00:14:05,053 --> 00:14:06,429
[SHIZUKA] How interesting.

279
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,724
A proxy war between the angels
and demons?

280
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,809
Quite the grandiose
affair indeed.

281
00:14:11,893 --> 00:14:13,311
And calling it a death game

282
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:15,813
certainly raises some red flags
in my eyes.

283
00:14:15,897 --> 00:14:17,899
Wait, if you think
it's a red flag,

284
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,901
does that mean
you're worried about me?

285
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:22,028
I think anyone would be,
in my shoes.

286
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:23,738
Who wants their neighbor
to get hurt?

287
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:25,239
[ABADDON] On that,

288
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:27,075
you live right next door,
don't you?

289
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,701
[SASAKI] So what if I do?

290
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:30,203
It just seems to me

291
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,537
you might have
taken a stronger hand

292
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:33,623
in making sure
she was all right over there.

293
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,416
Maybe then
she would have never met a demon

294
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,667
in the first place.

295
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:38,544
Hell, even if we had met,

296
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:39,629
maybe she wouldn't
have felt the need

297
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:40,838
to form a contract with me

298
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:43,424
if someone out there made her
feel safe to begin with.

299
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:46,302
Hey, you'd better be careful
what you say, Abaddon.

300
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,429
Has any of it been untrue?

301
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:49,472
Shush.

302
00:14:49,931 --> 00:14:51,808
Either way, I guess
it's better late than never

303
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,143
to get people like you
on the same side as us.

304
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:57,563
I would prefer to stay out of
such a dangerous game as that.

305
00:14:57,647 --> 00:14:59,357
I can't say that
I blame you there.

306
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,858
But didn't I tell you

307
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:02,360
about the wonderful perks
that come

308
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,362
from working with an angel
or demon?

309
00:15:04,946 --> 00:15:07,156
"Wishes beyond human
comprehension," I believe,

310
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,158
-is how you worded it.
-Huh.

311
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:10,910
But the two of us
aren't disciples,

312
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,036
so it's a moot point.

313
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:14,455
[ABADDON] My partner
sure seems to like you.

314
00:15:14,539 --> 00:15:16,624
That counts for a lot,
if you ask me.

315
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,001
If you play your cards right,

316
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:21,212
we might be able to work out
some sort of arrangement

317
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,880
where you receive
personal rewards

318
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:25,258
through the wishes
that I'll be granting her.

319
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:27,760
[SASAKI] I can only assume
other participants

320
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:28,970
in this death game

321
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,764
are undergoing
similar negotiations elsewhere.

322
00:15:31,848 --> 00:15:34,517
And that means
there are an awful lot of people

323
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,935
who might
quickly find their ways

324
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:37,728
into the halls of power.

325
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,355
It's only a matter of time

326
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:41,983
until the bureau catches wind
of what's going on here.

327
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,486
Even more importantly,

328
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,863
this concerns my neighbor,

329
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,948
who I've known
since she was a little kid.

330
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,702
[NEIGHBOR] Mm.

331
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:54,495
[SHIZUKA]
Dangerous though it may be...

332
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:55,580
Huh?

333
00:15:56,122 --> 00:15:59,083
...I must say, I am intrigued
by what you're offering.

334
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:00,710
Yeah, I'll bet you are,

335
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:01,878
and at your first chance

336
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:03,212
you're gonna ask him
to lift your curse.

337
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:05,214
-Isn't that right?
-Uh?

338
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:06,465
-[tires screeching]
-[SHIZUKA] What?!

339
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:08,551
How did you figure that out?

340
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,511
[SASAKI] Well,
it's kinda obvious.

341
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:13,306
Why such
an over-the-top reaction?

342
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:15,683
[ABADDON] You should be aware,

343
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,019
a lot of angels
are gonna know we're here

344
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:19,353
after what just happened.

345
00:16:21,022 --> 00:16:22,481
If you don't mind my asking,

346
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:24,525
are you partners
with any other disciples?

347
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:26,235
I'm afraid that's not
on the table

348
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:27,236
when you have a partner

349
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:29,697
with social anxiety
as severe as mine has.

350
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,991
Abaddon, I really wish
you'd think a little bit more

351
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,492
about my feelings
before you speak.

352
00:16:34,202 --> 00:16:35,328
[SASAKI] I see.

353
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,538
She's like Hoshizaki
in that way.

354
00:16:38,206 --> 00:16:40,875
I guess it's to be expected,
given her home life.

355
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:43,044
Thinking back,

356
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:45,922
I don't think I've ever seen her
hanging out with friends.

357
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,673
Certainly none have come over.

358
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:50,885
Funny.
I guess we're not so different.

359
00:16:51,886 --> 00:16:53,971
Though things have been better
lately on my end.

360
00:16:54,055 --> 00:16:56,474
Peeps has kept
my life fulfilling.

361
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:00,144
I've decided, going forward,

362
00:17:00,228 --> 00:17:01,479
I think I'd like
to work with you.

363
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:02,813
You really mean it?

364
00:17:02,897 --> 00:17:04,899
That's awesome news
for my side of the war!

365
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,359
[NEIGHBOR] You really
don't have to force yourself

366
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:07,652
to do anything.

367
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:09,612
I'll be able to
take care of things on my own.

368
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:12,657
[SASAKI] Might I ask
a rather blunt question?

369
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,533
What happens

370
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:16,285
when that six-winged angel
comes back?

371
00:17:16,953 --> 00:17:19,705
Do you think you'll be able
to handle her alone, Abaddon?

372
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:22,792
Well, if it was a 1v1,
I'm pretty confident

373
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,794
I could at least force the fight
into a stalemate.

374
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:27,296
Considering how many angels
they sent back there,

375
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,216
I don't think they're too keen
on letting you have that 1v1.

376
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,634
Do I have the wrong idea,

377
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,135
or are you worried
about this girl?

378
00:17:34,804 --> 00:17:36,347
Well, of course I'm worried.

379
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:38,766
Why would I have joined in
back there if I wasn't?

380
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:40,059
[gasps]

381
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:44,355
[ABADDON] Well, fortunately,

382
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:46,565
I managed to do a number
on their ranks.

383
00:17:46,649 --> 00:17:49,360
Assuming their disciples
aren't super dumb,

384
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:52,530
I doubt that they'll be coming
after us again any time soon,

385
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:56,075
especially not with an X factor
like you on our side.

386
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:57,702
[Sasaki sighs]

387
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,246
Though what I'd like most
from you isn't your strength.

388
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:02,164
It's your help
with interpersonal conflicts

389
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,541
within your own world.

390
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:07,044
They failed even after using
an angelic force of that size.

391
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:09,171
Not much point in
repeating that approach,

392
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:11,716
so I assume we'll see some
different tactics next time.

393
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,468
[SASAKI] So for now,
they're looking for physical aid

394
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:16,929
outside of
those quarantine spaces.

395
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:19,015
If he knew what Peeps could do,

396
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,225
I wonder if he'd be singing
the same tune.

397
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:23,811
I believe I understand,

398
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:26,439
but would you give me some time
to truly consider your offer?

399
00:18:26,522 --> 00:18:29,400
Sure! I'd appreciate any help
you can give me,

400
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:31,277
so you should take
all the time you need.

401
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:32,945
Very well then.

402
00:18:33,029 --> 00:18:34,905
By the way, Futari Shizuka,

403
00:18:34,989 --> 00:18:37,742
sorry to ask, but my neighbor
really should get home.

404
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:39,910
You need me to stop
by your place

405
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:42,246
just so we can drop off
this little girl?

406
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:44,457
[SASAKI]
Would you mind terribly?

407
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,001
[SHIZUKA] I'm gonna start
running a meter.

408
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:50,921
[SASAKI] Well, good night.

409
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:52,381
[car door closes]

410
00:19:01,766 --> 00:19:02,683
[neighbor grunts]

411
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:04,560
Even today,

412
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,521
he's still the reason I'm alive.

413
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:11,275
Just look at yourself.
What would he say

414
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:13,486
if he knew the sins
behind that smile?

415
00:19:14,195 --> 00:19:16,072
Maybe someone as kind as him
would have the right

416
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,449
to judge me for being a sinner,
but not you.

417
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:22,244
What time will he get back?

418
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:24,330
Will work keep him up late?

419
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:26,874
It seemed like he was busy,

420
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:29,335
so I might not
see him again today.

421
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:33,881
[ABADDON] But alas,
despite our little chat,

422
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:36,092
we weren't able to confirm
what the two of them are.

423
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:38,219
He's himself, that's all.

424
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:41,013
I don't see why anything else
should matter to me.

425
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,349
There's that
one-track mind again.

426
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:46,143
Try considering things
as if you were me.

427
00:19:46,769 --> 00:19:48,646
Then let me try
to put this in a different way.

428
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:49,980
We're not in a good position

429
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:51,899
to force them to share
details about themselves

430
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:53,359
they don't feel ready to share.

431
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:55,945
And I think if we try
to push them to open up,

432
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:58,656
it'll only make them
more closed off than before.

433
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:01,534
So instead, we should wait
until they share voluntarily.

434
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,328
I agree that's the best move
and all,

435
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:06,122
but I don't really think
you're one to talk,

436
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,040
considering how much
you've looked into his life

437
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:09,083
all on your own.

438
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,793
I have not. Don't lie!

439
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:13,379
[ABADDON] Then I must have
misunderstood some things,

440
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,506
like when you put your ear
to his wall.

441
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,843
Or how you sometimes peek
into his windows at night.

442
00:20:20,678 --> 00:20:22,138
Never tell him
about those things,

443
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,306
even if it's
with our lives on the line.

444
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:26,851
Oh, that's too bad then.

445
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,352
I was gonna
tell him all about it,

446
00:20:28,436 --> 00:20:31,105
but since you ordered me not to,
I guess I can't anymore.

447
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,857
[laughs]

448
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:34,900
[NEIGHBOR] I'm tired of this.

449
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,862
I wanna feel the man next door,

450
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:42,491
to fill my mind with him,
and bask in his warmth.

451
00:20:43,284 --> 00:20:45,119
Oh, Mister,

452
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,788
you're so wonderful.

453
00:20:48,539 --> 00:20:51,125
I wanna talk to you forever.

454
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:53,294
I wanna gaze at you forever.

455
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:56,172
I wanna listen to you forever.

456
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:59,717
[moaning]

457
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,889
Just the thought of him
makes me so happy.

458
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:07,558
I don't know
what I'm supposed to do.

459
00:21:08,184 --> 00:21:09,560
But now that I think,

460
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:11,020
who was that girl in the kimono

461
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,897
who was driving us around
anyway?

462
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:15,733
A coworker, so he told us,

463
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:18,235
but she was so small,
she could have been a child.

464
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:21,405
Did you catch anything about her
I should know?

465
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:24,658
Nah. But she was
hanging out with him,

466
00:21:24,742 --> 00:21:27,161
so I figure
she's not normal either.

467
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,621
Yeah, that makes sense.

468
00:21:29,330 --> 00:21:31,332
-Hmm.
-What's the matter?

469
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,167
You went quiet all of a sudden.

470
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,585
It's nothing. I'm fine.

471
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:38,047
[sighs]

472
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:42,259
[NEIGHBOR] It's okay.
He and I are kindred spirits.

473
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,261
We're the same.

474
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:46,639
And next time,

475
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,974
I-I'll be the one to save him.

476
00:21:49,892 --> 00:21:52,895
Then, once we've been smeared
in each other's blood

477
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,230
from head to toe,

478
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,982
we'll be closer
than ever before.

479
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,276
What a lovely thought.

480
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:03,781
Although, the next time we meet,

481
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:07,117
I need to find out more
about who that girl is,

482
00:22:07,201 --> 00:22:08,953
and why she's with him.

483
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:12,623
[♪ closing theme song playing]

